    "question": "Dallas and Austin went to the pick-your-own orchard. Dallas picked 14 bags of apples and 9 bags of pears. Austin picked 6 bags of apples more than Dallas, and 5 fewer bags of pears than Dallas. How many bags of fruit did Austin pick, in total?",
    "gold": "24",
    "answer": "He picked 14+6=<<14+6=20>>20 bags of apples.\nHe picked 9-5=<<9-5=4>>4 bags of pears.\nHe picked 20+4=<<20+4=24>>24 bags of fruit in total.\n#### 24"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of bags of fruit Austin picked, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of bags of apples Austin picked.\n2. Calculate the number of bags of pears Austin picked.\n3. Add the number of bags of apples and pears Austin picked to find the total number of bags of fruit he picked.\n\nFirst, we know that Dallas picked 14 bags of apples. Since Austin picked 6 more bags of apples than Dallas, we can calculate the number of bags of apples Austin picked as follows:\n\\[\n14 + 6 = 20\n\\]\nSo, Austin picked 20 bags of apples.\n\nNext, we know that Dallas picked 9 bags of pears. Since Austin picked 5 fewer bags of pears than Dallas, we can calculate the number of bags of pears Austin picked as follows:\n\\[\n9 - 5 = 4\n\\]\nSo, Austin picked 4 bags of pears.\n\nNow, we add the number of bags of apples and pears Austin picked to find the total number of bags of fruit he picked:\n\\[\n20 + 4 = 24\n\\]\nTherefore, the total number of bags of fruit Austin picked is \\boxed{24}.",
